{% doc %}
  Our own merch, offered in the cart. A separate tier from the vendor upsell,
  deliberately.

  WHY IT IS NOT PART OF THE VENDOR UPSELL. That tier's argument is that a
  supplier already in the cart adds no extra parcel. Merch still adds a parcel —
  it is printed and posted on its own — so it cannot borrow that line.

  It must also never be counted toward a free-shipping threshold. Those
  thresholds belong to suppliers and are cleared by adding more of THEIR items;
  a sticker we post separately moves a supplier's cart total without moving
  their shipping at all. Quoting it as progress toward free shipping would be a
  promise with nothing behind it, which is the failure the shipping work exists
  to prevent.

  IT NOW HAS ITS OWN SHIPPING ARGUMENT, AND IT IS THE BETTER ONE. As of 8 Aug
  every product in this collection carries its measured postage in its price and
  sits in a delivery profile with a $0 rate, so merch adds a parcel at no cost
  to the shopper. This tier used to say nothing about shipping because there was
  nothing good to say; there is now, and it leads with it.

  THAT CLAIM IS ONLY AS TRUE AS THE `merch` AGENT. That agent prices and
  free-ships exactly the merch it has a measured shipping cost for, and
  deliberately excludes the rest. A product tagged into this collection between
  agent runs is in this list, and is not yet free to ship. The window is up to
  six hours and the fix is to run the agent, not to soften the copy.

  RENDERS NOTHING UNTIL THE COLLECTION HAS SOMETHING IN IT. The collection can
  be created empty and this stays invisible; the moment a product is published
  into it the tier appears, with no deploy. That is the point — the merch does
  not exist yet.

  @param {string} collection - Handle of the merch collection.
  @param {string} [heading] - Section heading.
  @param {string} [blurb] - One line under the heading.
  @param {number} [limit] - How many to show. Default 2.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign merch_handle = collection | default: 'yoink-merch'
  assign merch = collections[merch_handle]
  assign max_items = limit | default: 2 | plus: 0

  comment
    Everything already in the cart is excluded, so the tier disappears once the
    add-on has been added rather than nagging for a second one.
  endcomment
  assign in_cart = ','
  for line in cart.items
    assign in_cart = in_cart | append: line.product.id | append: ','
  endfor

  assign available_count = 0
  for item in merch.products limit: 12
    assign probe = ',' | append: item.id | append: ','
    unless in_cart contains probe or item.available == false
      assign available_count = available_count | plus: 1
    endunless
  endfor
-%}

{%- if merch != blank and available_count > 0 -%}
  {{ 'aj-cart-upsell.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  <section class="aj-cart-upsell aj-cart-merch" aria-labelledby="aj-cart-merch-heading">
    <h3 class="aj-cart-upsell__heading" id="aj-cart-merch-heading">
      {{ heading | default: 'Make it yours' | escape }}
    </h3>

    {%- assign blurb_text = blurb | default: 'If it has got our name on it, we pay the postage. Ships on its own, at no charge.' -%}
    {%- if blurb_text != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        TWO FACTS, IN THE ORDER THEY MATTER. The offer first: merch ships free,
        which since 8 Aug is true of everything in this collection — its price
        carries the measured postage and it sits in a $0 delivery profile.

        The old line led with provenance — "ours, not a supplier's" — which was
        both the weaker fact and one this store cannot claim: merch is printed
        on demand by Printify, and the same wording was removed from the
        homepage and collection page for that reason.

        The separate-parcel note stays, demoted to a clause. It is still true
        and still worth saying, because being told up front costs nothing and
        being surprised by it later is a support ticket. It is just no longer
        the headline, now that arriving separately costs the shopper nothing.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="aj-cart-merch__blurb">{{ blurb_text | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <ul class="aj-cart-upsell__list" role="list">
      {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
      {%- for item in merch.products limit: 12 -%}
        {%- assign probe = ',' | append: item.id | append: ',' -%}
        {%- if in_cart contains probe or item.available == false -%}
          {%- continue -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if shown >= max_items -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
        {% render 'aj-cart-upsell-item', item: item %}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </section>
{%- endif -%}
